# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
# Saver profile: copy to .env and edit WORKER. See the measured workload limits.
# It selects the dedicated saver profile. The KV pool is still shared.
#
# Start and warm the intended sidecars before SparkQwen; repeat their work
# during a long Qwen request to check headroom. See docs/MEMORY-PROFILES.md.
# The sidecars themselves are separate installations maintained outside this
# repository; ./start.sh neither installs nor manages them.

# ssh destination of the second Spark (rank 1). Passwordless ssh, and its user
# can run docker. Its address on the direct cable also makes the one-time copy
# of the 95 GiB checkpoint much faster.
WORKER=you@worker.example

# Where the checkpoint lives (95 GiB). The same absolute path is used on both
# Sparks. Default: $HOME/models/sparkqwen
#MODEL_ROOT=/srv/models/sparkqwen

# Eight scheduler slots, each limited to 262,144 tokens including output.
# The BF16 KV pool is shared. See docs/MEMORY-PROFILES.md for capacity guidance,
# sidecar workloads and peak headroom; eight complete contexts are not reserved.
PROFILE=saver-8x262k
MODE=spark

# The profile enables display-memory borrowing on both ranks. Keep the same
# utilization on both hosts. Override only after checking peak memory under
# concurrent Qwen and sidecar load; idle free memory is not a sidecar budget.
#GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.74

# start.sh pulls ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkqwen:<install tree> for this
# checkout and builds from source only if that tag is not published.
# PULL=0 always builds from source.
#PULL=0
# Parallel compile jobs for a source build; lower it if the build runs out of memory.
#ATLAS_BUILD_JOBS=4

# Only for private Hugging Face mirrors; the pinned checkpoint is public.
#HF_TOKEN=

# Resolve each node's active RDMA interface independently. With no overrides,
# exactly one matching IPv4 subnet pair is required; ambiguous discovery stops.
# ./start.sh fabric checks selection without Docker, downloads or model changes.
# Override each host independently (the same physical port number is not required).
# List ALL intended rails, in matching peer order; extra siblings are not added.
#LEADER_FABRIC_HCA=rocep1s0f1,roceP2p1s0f1
#WORKER_FABRIC_HCA=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0
#LEADER_FABRIC_INTERFACE=enp1s0f1np1
#WORKER_FABRIC_INTERFACE=enp1s0f0np0
# FABRIC_HCA / FABRIC_INTERFACE remain shared fallbacks for either unset side.
# LEADER_ADDRESS, if set, must belong to the selected leader interface.
#LEADER_ADDRESS=192.0.2.1
